  "title": "Juicy French Style Pork Tenderloin",
  "description": "The main ingredients in this dish are meat, mayonnaise, cheese and onion, lots of onion.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I lived in France more than 10 years. My husband is French but neither he or his parents have heard of this dish. The French don't even suspect that this dish is called French style meat, but Russians eat this meat and know that it truly is \"French style meat\".</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21436,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1656287299436} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21436-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Juicy French Style Pork Tenderloin</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7305-3.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tThe main ingredients in this dish are meat, mayonnaise, cheese and onion, lots of onion.\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>6 pork tenderloin chops</li><li>Salt and freshly ground black pepper (to taste)</li><li>1-2 onion</li><li>200 g cheese (shredded )</li><li>5-6 Tbsp mayonnaise</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Preheat oven to 380 degrees F. Line medium baking dish with aluminum foil.</li><li>Place each piece of meat between two sheets of plastic wrap and pound with the flat side of meat tenderizer until about 1/4 inch thick. Season both sides with salt and pepper.   <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7277.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Lay the meat out on the baking dish. Peel and cut the onion (half-moon). Arrange the onion on top of the pork. Sprinkle with shredded cheese. Spread mayonnaise all over the meat.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7278-2.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Bake for about 40 minutes until golden brown. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7292-2.Blog_-1-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Main Dish</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
